n dollar  fine they clawed back sixty million  dollars from executives you know what do  you make of that take that it really  hasn't hurt them that much yeah it's  when this initially came out I think a  lot of people looked at the size of the  fine and looked at the amount of money  you know fees that the bank charged  customers it was like two and a half  million and said oh this is a small  thing but it's sort of built on itself  Washington DC got involved lawmakers got  involved and they they brought Stumpf  down to DC for not one but two hearings  first in front of the Senate then in  front of the House Financial Services  Committee so it's it's sort of picked on  picked up a life of its own and and  built on itself and the scrutiny and the  pressure on Stumpf really just has been  building
 

